{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls is randomly and independently painted either black or white with equal probability. What is the probability that every ball is different in color from more than half of the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/756452b590f2e00c2cb604474a71a2ff1e27a5f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{64}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{5}{16}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"393\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that for this restriction to be true, there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls of each color. There are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a901d5103f4658787ce321610aa348a76ea79fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^6 = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> ways to color the balls, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b47e04a4e8c7ad9f5064f255826fe7e0458f40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${6 \\choose 3} = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> ways for three balls chosen to be painted white.  Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/29613cd927dbbcd6f4c5ff2564cb2d7e4f3a4f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20}{64} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{5}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"118\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>-Aidensharp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For this restriction to be upheld, there must be three black and three white balls. One such way for this to occur is the arrangement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc087c53762735458008f90342122543dc0bbc07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BBBWWW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" />, which has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/361ea76f684eb7847335f9a71099e0089811016e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" /> probability of occuring. However, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5f0b58c7c4e10d2137ba33cf7c183eab601f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6!}{3!\\cdot{3!}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"39\" /> ways to arrange the three black and three white balls, meaning that the answer is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bcae52023eff1784309f18ed00c7310b5b0b70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{64}\\cdot{\\frac{6!}{3!\\cdot{3!}}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{5}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"176\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To get every ball different in color from more than half of the other 5 balls, we must have 3 black balls and 3 white balls.\n</p><p>Following from the binomial theorem, this happens with probability\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd15f1f8a9850aa66568b488c77a4f76f92cbf57.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\binom{6}{3} \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right)^3 \\left( 1 - \\frac{1}{2} \\right)^{6-3} = \\frac{5}{16} . \\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fc836446412bb34cfff01ea3aca22d09c06754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{5}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"71\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/95aRRJ3jMqo\">https://youtu.be/95aRRJ3jMqo</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zq3UPu4nwsE?t=707\">https://youtu.be/zq3UPu4nwsE?t=707</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5m8zYiOagCY\">https://youtu.be/5m8zYiOagCY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A\">2021 Fall AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n<